{"duration_api_ms":163898,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cc1e7d34-0135-4bad-8fce-13c51f851780","total_cost_usd":0.214864,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14390,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15730,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10488},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15730,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15730,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14390,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.214864,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10488,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially a one-dimensional gamma sweep at D≈3.36-3.37 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg. Flux rises about 24 kW/m2 per degree of steeper entry and bondline temperature falls about 10-14 K per degree. The front is closed on the steep side by max_g (limit about 12.0, reached near gamma -3.58) and on the large-D side by heatshield mass fraction (margin near 0 at D≈3.385). Cone 70 is the upper bound. Bluntness above about 1.2 at cone 70 returns 'no geometry' from surrogate extrapolation (4 failures at 1.22-1.24).\",\"evidence\":[\"C-af5b99c2201c through C-df105fb625ce: at D 3.36-3.37, bluntness 1.2, cone 70, flux runs 243.6k to 277.1k and bondline 407.4 K to 391.7 K as gamma goes from -2.2 to -3.55. Both trends are smooth and near-linear.\",\"C-2a109f1c4205 (gamma -3.58) has max_g margin -0.0005, and C-df105fb625ce (gamma -3.55) has margin +0.0037. The g limit therefore sits near gamma -3.57 at D 3.36.\",\"C-ba7e63c2eae5 (D 3.2), C-757eacb03d61 (D 3.3) and C-77cd7361eded (D 3.1) all have higher flux and bondline temperature than D 3.36 at similar gamma. Larger D is better, and it is capped by mass fraction: margin 0.0149 at D 3.36 and 0.0090 at 3.37, extrapolating to zero near 3.385.\",\"C-de59f8abeee6, C-ae614eb129f2, C-fc8f94cd132b and C-d5f231dc1870: bluntness 1.22-1.24 at cone 70 fails on the cd_fore hull. C-0a3bfd5f8237 (b 1.15, c 69) and C-19b8d4ea2ba7 (b 1.1, c 68) are slightly worse than b 1.2, c 70 at the same gamma.\",\"C-ee99f55de428 and C-50a0a474d0f6 (small D, low bluntness) have flux of 0.75-1.5 MW/m2 and bondline above the 450 K limit. Only the large, blunt, high-cone corner is competitive.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux falls with larger nose radius and lower ballistic coefficient (larger D, higher drag). Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which falls for steeper entry and lower flux. Peak g rises with gamma steepness, and slightly with D at fixed gamma. The best trade-off is the largest D the mass limit allows, bluntness and cone at their buildable maxima, and gamma at the g limit. In hypervolume terms 1 K of bondline temperature is worth about 0.006, while 10 kW/m2 of flux is worth only about 0.004. So this round nudges D up to 3.38 (about -1.3 kW/m2 and -0.3 K versus 3.37), pushes gamma toward the g limit, and extends the shallow-gamma flux end. Small bluntness, cone and D probes are included to check whether the corner can move.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g and mass-fraction limits are extrapolated linearly. The D 3.38 mass margin is estimated at about +0.003, and D 3.385 is nearly zero. Gamma -3.565 at D 3.38 is within about 0.001 in g of the limit. The hull boundary for bluntness above 1.2 is unknown and b 1.21 may fail. Predictions for shallow gamma below -2.2 extrapolate the flux and temperature slopes, and curvature could shift them by a few kelvin.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the front: extends the lowest flux extreme at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":226500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the extrapolated slope beyond the shallowest evaluated gamma (-2.2) and sets the low-flux front extreme.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the shallow-gamma part of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage between -1.5 and -2.2 on the low-flux side.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the shallow-gamma part of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage between -1.5 and -2.2 on the low-flux side.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Small step from the shallowest evaluated front point, with D raised to 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D 3.38 shift against C-af5b99c2201c.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage, and a check of the D effect on flux and bondline.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.85},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-to-steep front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage with the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-to-steep front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af5b99c2201c\",\"rationale\":\"Steep-side front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Steep-side front point at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Steep-side front point at D 3.38, close to the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Reference corner point at D 3.38, gamma -3.5. D is raised from 3.36 with a small g penalty and a small gain in flux and bondline.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-f579cc1dc4f8 if the mass margin holds at D 3.38.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-df105fb625ce\",\"rationale\":\"Corner design at D 3.38 and gamma -3.55, where g margin is expected to be about +0.003.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Would dominate C-df105fb625ce if feasible, and probes the g margin versus D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-df105fb625ce\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes gamma to the estimated g limit at D 3.38 for the lowest bondline temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary at D 3.38. Bondline temperature is the most valuable hypervolume lever, so a feasible result here gains directly.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Probes the bluntness hull limit slightly above 1.2 (1.22 failed). Higher bluntness lowers flux a little.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds whether b 1.21 is inside the cd_fore hull. If so it slightly improves the corner; if not, it sharpens the boundary estimate.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly lower bluntness as a safe-side check of the bluntness sensitivity around 1.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a local gradient in bluntness at cone 70 and D 3.38, and may show a mass-fraction benefit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f579cc1dc4f8\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes D to the mass-fraction edge (predicted margin about 0.0002) for a further small gain in flux and bondline.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests where the heatshield mass-fraction constraint becomes active, which sets the D ceiling for the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0a3bfd5f8237\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69 with bluntness 1.2 at D 3.38. This is inside the sampled cone/bluntness region and separates the cone effect from the bluntness effect seen in C-0a3bfd5f8237.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Clarifies whether cone angle 70 is strictly best or whether cone 69 helps g or mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":122632,"type":"result","duration_ms":163936,"uuid":"9c19b62b-619e-46c7-a4e3-9c43eb51cbf4","ttft_stream_ms":1506,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":1506,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
